#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""image-first-boot: the FIXED independent boot-and-hardening test suite for `kind=image-first-boot` (golden guest images).

Contract with the attestor (blueprints/build/repo/ou-test-attest, review 7 H-3; interface read from branch fixes-r7): ou-test-attest copies the image to a private work
directory, hashes it, and runs THIS program from its root-owned lib directory (<lib>/image-first-boot, installed by root from this repo, never from the builder's
output) as `image-first-boot <image.qcow2>` with a scrubbed environment (OU_TEST_KIND, OU_TEST_WORK). Exit 0 = every check passed, 1 = at least one check failed,
anything else = infrastructure error (NO attestation is produced for it). The attestor, not this program and not the builder, signs the result; this program
prints a log that the attestor hashes. The builder only gets to ASK for a run and cannot influence a verdict: it supplies neither the expected values, nor the
callback server, nor the SMBIOS secret (all are generated here, fresh, per run).

What it does (all under qemu TCG, no KVM needed, user-mode network with `restrict=on`: the guest can reach only the throw-away ICS simulator through one guestfwd):
  stage OFFLINE  static hardening checks over the extracted pristine image (tests/staticchecks.py)
  stage A        boot 1 with a valid bootstrap record: probes while the callback is in flight (default-deny loaded, no ssh banner, agent not running), HMAC verified
                 by the simulator, enrollment surface (pinned TLS fingerprint, one-time token, no unsigned / non-allowlisted execution), graceful shutdown,
                 offline inspection of the disk and the persistent journal (secret and token absent everywhere; sealed; unit disabled)
  stage B        reboot of the same disk with the SMBIOS values STILL present: the sealed bootstrap does not run and does not call the ICS a second time
  stage C        wrong certificate pin in SMBIOS: no report is sent (the simulator sees a TLS handshake and zero HTTP requests), agent never starts
  stage D        impostor ICS (right certificate, acknowledgement made with the wrong secret): the guest refuses it, never starts the agent
  stage E        wrong HMAC secret in the guest (clone / stolen serial): the ICS side rejects the report, nothing is enrolled
Requires: qemu-system-x86_64, qemu-img, openssl, debugfs (e2fsprogs), sfdisk, python3 + `cryptography`; journalctl is used when present (best effort)."""
